column19:
You are right about it starting on 41, but chances are that that is its intended behavior, with a bit of context that is more clear:<p><pre><code>  #define ARRAYSIZE 42

  int array[ARRAYSIZE];

  void f() {
     for (i=ARRAYSIZE; i --> 0;) {
       printf("%d
", array[i]);
     }
  }
</code></pre>
If it were to start at 42 you'd be referencing the array outside of its bounds.
